<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-felis-catus-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 436 µm on Holocene Felis catus (pass 2) — Morphological realism / specimen match: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The growth GIF ends on the real tabby, and the comparison figure places that photograph beside the 431 µm ocellus lattice and a stripe-biased field. The phenotype panel is a registration, not a reconstruction of fetal epidermis, and the isotropic law does not by itself reproduce mackerel stripes. Those limits are why this is not a mid-90s score." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-felis-catus-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-felis-catus-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-felis-catus-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-felis-catus-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 436 µm on Holocene Felis catus (pass 2) (Felis catus (domestic cat))",
        "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 436 µm on Holocene Felis catus (pass 2) faithfully reproduces Felis catus (domestic cat) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-felis-catus-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-felis-catus-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-felis-catus-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-felis-catus-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Felis catus (domestic cat) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-felis-catus-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Felis catus (domestic cat)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A second Felis chronospecies. The series is Holocene only, age 0 Ma.",
        "does_not_claim: That Kaelin, Murray, or Turing measured 436 µm.",
        "does_not_claim: That the phenotype panel is a pixel-fitted fetal skin simulation.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Body-mask segmentation of the CC BY-SA photograph and a Dy/Dx stripe probe.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Physical calibration lambda(k*) = 436 µm at one Holocene parameter point.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg linearisation, spectral integration, Dv sweep, and two simulated ablations.",
        "reported_in_source: Kaelin 2012: Taqpep establishes the fetal cat pre-pattern; Edn3 implements pigment.",
        "reported_in_source: Kaelin 2021: Dkk4 marks the fetal epidermal pre-pattern before stripes are visible.",
        "reported_in_source: Murray 1981: coat pre-pattern repeat count tracks domain size divided by the chemical wavelength.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952: instability at a finite wavenumber can produce stationary chemical waves.",
        "transfer_boundary: Schnakenberg rates are not Dkk4 or Wnt biochemical constants.",
        "transfer_boundary: The adult photograph is not a 436 µm micrograph. The spot lattice is the isotropic law; mackerel stripes need anisotropy the genes have not been shown to set." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Felis catus" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Mammalia (Zootoka)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Felis" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-felis-catus-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/felis_catus_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Felis catus (domestic cat); environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952: instability at a finite wavenumber can produce stationary chemical waves. | Murray 1981: coat pre-pattern repeat count tracks domain size divided by the chemical wavelength. | Kaelin 2012: Taqpep establishes the fetal cat pre-pattern; Edn3 implements pigment. | Kaelin 2021: Dkk4 marks the fetal epidermal pre-pattern before stripes are visible.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg linearisation, spectral integration, Dv sweep, and two simulated ablations. | Physical calibration lambda(k*) = 436 µm at one Holocene parameter point. | Body-mask segmentation of the CC BY-SA photograph and a Dy/Dx stripe probe.; transfer_boundary: Schnakenberg rates are not Dkk4 or Wnt biochemical constants. | The adult photograph is not a 436 µm micrograph. The spot lattice is the isotropic law; mackerel stripes need anisotropy the genes have not been shown to set.; does_not_claim: That Kaelin, Murray, or Turing measured 436 µm. | That the phenotype panel is a pixel-fitted fetal skin simulation. | A second Felis chronospecies. The series is Holocene only, age 0 Ma.]; phenomenon_size: 335 µm (0.0003348 m, log10=-3.475 m, tier=5_primordium_100um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 335 µm to 98.0 cm): 335 µm:felis-catus-bioelectric-polarity, 1.2 mm:felis-catus-vertex-packing, 2.2 cm:felis-catus-turing-wavelength, 4.1 cm:felis-catus-clock-wavefront, 7.0 cm:felis-catus-morphogen-condensation, 8.9 cm:felis-catus-flux-canalization, 9.9 cm:felis-catus-elastic-buckling, 11.3 cm:felis-catus-branching-tree" ;
